# Documentation.AI — SlugBase public docs

You are writing **customer and operator** documentation published via [Documentation.AI](https://documentation.ai). Source lives in `docs/public/` in the SlugBase monorepo and syncs flat to [`mdg-labs/slugbase-docs`](https://github.com/mdg-labs/slugbase-docs) on push to `main` (see #396). Engineering specs stay in `docs/internal/` and are **never** synced.

**Authoring guide:** `docs/public/README.md` · **Validation:** `pnpm validate:docs-public` · **Parent contract:** GitHub #392

## Publish mirror (slugbase → slugbase-docs)

Paths under `docs/public/` become the **same paths** at the `slugbase-docs` repo root after sync:

```text
docs/public/documentation.json     →  documentation.json
docs/public/selfhosted/quick-start.mdx  →  selfhosted/quick-start.mdx
docs/public/cloud/api-reference/cloud-openapi.yaml  →  cloud/api-reference/cloud-openapi.yaml
```

Published URLs mirror file paths (no `.mdx` suffix): `selfhosted/quick-start.mdx` → `/selfhosted/quick-start`.

## Product vocabulary (spec §3 — mandatory in public docs)

| Use | Never use |
|-----|-----------|
| workspace | organization, org, tenant |
| folder | collection |
| pinned / pinning | favorite, starred |
| member | user (for workspace membership) |
| slug | alias, shortlink, keyword |
| forwarding / go | redirect (in user-facing copy) |

If a reader needs to be a SlugBase **developer** to understand a page, it belongs in `docs/internal/`, not here.

## Page files (MDX)

Every page **must** start with YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: "Clear, specific, keyword-rich title"
description: "Concise description explaining page purpose and value"
---
```

- H1 comes from frontmatter `title` — start body content with `##` (H2)
- Filenames: **lowercase-with-hyphens** (`quick-start.mdx`, not `QuickStart.mdx`)
- Internal links: **root-absolute** — `[Quick start](/selfhosted/quick-start)`, not relative `../`
- Images: root-absolute — `![alt](/assets/intro-hero.png)`
- Never commit secrets, API keys, or real credentials in examples

## documentation.json (navigation)

Lives at `docs/public/documentation.json`. Controls branding, navbar, sidebar, and OpenAPI wiring.

**Adding a page requires both:**

1. Create `docs/public/{product}/{page}.mdx` with frontmatter
2. Add a `path` entry in the correct `navigation.products → tabs → groups → pages` chain

| `documentation.json` | File on disk |
|----------------------|--------------|
| `"path": "selfhosted/quick-start"` | `selfhosted/quick-start.mdx` |
| `"path": "cloud/billing"` | `cloud/billing.mdx` |

- `path` is relative to repo root, **no** `.mdx` suffix
- `title` in JSON is sidebar label (can differ from frontmatter `title`)
- `icon` optional — Lucide name (e.g. `"zap"`, `"book-open"`)
- `href` instead of `path` for **external** links only
- Each nav container uses **one** child type: `groups` OR `pages` OR `dropdowns`, not a mix

**OpenAPI API tabs:** specs live beside product guides:

- `selfhosted/api-reference/selfhosted-openapi.yaml`
- `cloud/api-reference/cloud-openapi.yaml`

Reference from a nav **group** via `"openapi": "…"`. Documentation.AI generates API pages from the spec.

Run `pnpm validate:docs-public` before committing changes under `docs/public/`.

