## Core writing principles

### Language and style

- Clear, direct language for technical audiences
- Second person ("you") for instructions; active voice; present tense for current states
- Define jargon on first use; consistent terminology
- Concise sentences; parallel structure in lists and headings

### Content organization

- Lead with the most important information
- Progressive disclosure: basics before advanced topics
- Numbered steps for procedures; prerequisites before instructions
- Descriptive, keyword-rich headings (H2 → H3 → H4)
- Verification steps so readers can confirm success

### User-centered approach

- Focus on user goals and outcomes, not internal implementation
- Anticipate common questions; include troubleshooting for likely failures
- Write for scannability: headings, lists, callouts, white space

## Documentation.AI components

**Attribute naming:** kebab-case (`param-type`, `default-open`, `show-lines`). Boolean attributes: `required="true"` or `horizontal={true}`.

**Icons:** Lucide names without suffix — `icon="zap"`, `icon="book-open"` ([Lucide icons](https://lucide.dev/icons/)).

### Callouts

Use `<Callout kind="info|tip|alert|danger|success">` for supplementary, best-practice, caution, high-risk, and confirmation content.

### Code

- Fenced blocks with language tag; optional `title="filename.ext"`
- `<CodeGroup>` for multi-language equivalents
- `<Request>` / `<Response>` for API endpoint sidebar examples
- Complete, runnable examples with realistic (non-secret) data

### Structure

- `<Steps>` for sequential procedures (prefer over long ordered lists)
- `<Tabs>` for platform-specific or alternative approaches
- `<Expandable>` / `<ExpandableGroup>` for progressive disclosure
- `<Card title="…" href="…">` inside `<Columns>` for navigation grids
- `<ParamField>` / `<ResponseField>` for API parameters and responses
- `<Update>` for changelogs and release notes
- Mermaid for flowcharts and sequence diagrams

### Component selection

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Page structure | Markdown H2–H4 |
| Procedures | `<Steps>` |
| Platform variants | `<Tabs>` |
| Multi-language code | `<CodeGroup>` |
| API params/responses | `<ParamField>`, `<ResponseField>`, `<Request>`, `<Response>` |
| Highlights | `<Callout>` |
| Navigation grids | `<Card>` in `<Columns>` |
| Media | `<Image>`, `<Video>`, `<Iframe>` |

